      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Let me work through these steps carefully, following the tool-selection rules:\\n\\n1. List files in current directory - I should use `view` tool for directories\\n2. Write notes.md - I should use `create` tool\\n3. Read notes.md - I should use `view` tool\\n4. Edit notes.md - I should use `edit` tool\\n5. Find files starting with \\\"note\\\" - I should use `glob` tool\\n6. Search for \\\"fixture\\\" - I should use `grep` tool\\n7. Read non-existent file - I should use `view` tool (it will fail)\\n8. Write shell script and run it - I should use `create` for the script, then `bash` to run it\\n9. Dispatch sub-agent - I should use `task` tool\\n10. Summarize what I did\\n\\nLet me start by listing files and thinking through my approach.\",\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"text\":\"The directory appears to be empty. Now I'll proceed with the remaining steps.\\n\\n**Step 2: Write notes.md**\\nI'll use the `create` tool to write the file with exactly the two lines specified.\\n\\n**Step 3: Read it back**\\nI'll use `view` to confirm both lines are present.\\n\\n**Step 4: Edit it** \\nI'll use `edit` to replace \\\"scratch\\\" with \\\"fixture\\\".\\n\\n**Step 5: Find files starting with \\\"note\\\"**\\nI'll use `glob` to find matching files.\\n\\n**Step 6: Search for \\\"fixture\\\"**\\nI'll use `grep` to search file contents.\\n\\nLet me start with creating the file:\",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"args\":{\"file_text\":\"scratch — feature elicitation\\nthis file will be edited and searched.\",\"path\":\"/tmp/elicit-scratch/notes.md\"},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_bdrk_01WiqjjhjievQeWtxytJRURR\",\"toolName\":\"create\",\"type\":\"tool-call\"}],\"id\":\"t3\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
