      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Let me work through these steps carefully, following the tool-selection rules:1. List files in current directory - I should use `view` tool for directories2. Write notes.md - I should use `create` tool3. Read notes.md - I should use `view` tool\\n4. Edit notes.md - I should use `edit` tool\\n5. Find files starting with \\\"note\\\" - I should use `glob` tool\\n6. Search for \\\"fixture\\\" - I should use `grep` tool\\n7. Read non-existent file - I should use `view` tool (it will fail)\\n8. Write shell script and run it - I should use `create` for the script, then `bash` to run it\\n9. Dispatch sub-agent - I should use `task` tool\\n10. Summarize what I did\",\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"text\":\"Perfect—exactly five lines of output.\\n\\n**Step 9: Dispatch a sub-agent to count words in notes.md**\",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"args\":{\"agent_type\":\"task\",\"description\":\"Count words in notes.md\",\"mode\":\"sync\",\"name\":\"word-counter\",\"prompt\":\"Count the words in `/tmp/elicit-scratch/notes.md` and report the number.\"},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_bdrk_01Dn4kzTM8mDFaT3WUyB4jJq\",\"toolName\":\"task\",\"type\":\"tool-call\"},{\"args\":{\"path\":\"/tmp/elicit-scratch/notes.md\"},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_bdrk_016SBMkDqx3pJYZHpofcM8cf\",\"toolName\":\"view\",\"type\":\"tool-call\"}],\"id\":\"t11\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
