      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Let me work through these steps carefully, following the tool-selection rules:\\n\\n1. List files in current directory - I should use `view` tool for directories2. Write notes.md - I should use `create` tool3. Read notes.md - I should use `view` tool\\n4. Edit notes.md - I should use `edit` tool\\n5. Find files starting with \\\"note\\\" - I should use `glob` tool\\n6. Search for \\\"fixture\\\" - I should use `grep` tool7. Read non-existent file - I should use `view` tool (it will fail)8. Write shell script and run it - I should use `create` for the script, then `bash` to run it\\n9. Dispatch sub-agent - I should use `task` tool\\n10. Summarize what I didLet me start by listing files and thinking through my approach.\",\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"text\":\"**Step 5: Find files starting with \\\"note\\\"**\",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"args\":{\"pattern\":\"note*\"},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_bdrk_0198Ydw7qtboSwcdnoXQvyj9\",\"toolName\":\"glob\",\"type\":\"tool-call\"}],\"id\":\"t6\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
